.SH NAME
ns\(hyslapd \- The main Directory Server daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ns-slapd
\-D configdir [\fI\-d debuglevel\fR] [\fI\-i pidlogfile\fR] [\fI\-v\fR] [\fI\-V\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ns\(hyslapd launches the LDAP Directory Server 
.PP
.\" TeX users may be more comfortable with the \fB<whatever>\fP and
.\" \fI<whatever>\fP escape sequences to invoke bold face and italics, 
.\" respectively.
.SH OPTIONS
A summary of options is included below:
.TP
.B \-v
Show version of program.
.TP
.B \-D configdir
Specifies the configuration directory pointing at the instance
to be started (e.g. /etc/dirsrv/slapd\(hylocalhost)
.TP
.B \-d debuglevel
Specifies the debug level to be used. The value is a bitmask: add
(or bitwise\-OR) the levels you want. The same bit values are used by
.B nsslapd\-errorlog\-level
(error log) and, for the levels noted below,
.B nsslapd\-accesslog\-level
(access log).
.sp
.B Configurable logging levels
(these select extra messages for a given area):
.sp
.nf
     1  (0x00000001)  Trace function calls
     2  (0x00000002)  Packet handling / packet dump
     4  (0x00000004)  Heavy trace debugging (args)
     8  (0x00000008)  Connection management
    16  (0x00000010)  Packets sent and received (BER)
    32  (0x00000020)  Search filter processing
    64  (0x00000040)  Config file processing
   128  (0x00000080)  Access control list processing
   256  (0x00000100)  Stats log connections/operations (access log)
   512  (0x00000200)  Stats log entries sent (access log)
  1024  (0x00000400)  Shell database tracing
  2048  (0x00000800)  Entry parsing
  4096  (0x00001000)  Housekeeping / housekeeping thread
  8192  (0x00002000)  Replication
 16384  (0x00004000)  Default / summary error messages (ALWAYS)
 32768  (0x00008000)  Entry cache debugging
 65536  (0x00010000)  Plugin debugging
131072  (0x00020000)  Timing (unused; retained for compatibility)
262144  (0x00040000)  Access control summary
524288  (0x00080000)  Database (ldbm) debugging
1048576 (0x00100000)  Password policy debugging
.fi
.sp
Levels
.B 256
and
.B 512
apply to the access log
.RB ( nsslapd\-accesslog\-level ),
not the error log.
.sp
.B Severity levels
(EMERG, ALERT, CRIT, ERR, WARNING, NOTICE, INFO, DEBUG) refine the
meaning of default error messages. They are
.B not
administrator\-configurable log filters; do not set
.B nsslapd\-errorlog\-level
to only one of these values expecting to filter by severity.
.sp
Example: enable default messages plus ACL and replication debugging:
.sp
.nf
  16384 + 128 + 8192 = 24704
.fi
.sp
See also the error log levels and format documentation:
.br
https://www.port389.org/docs/389ds/design/errorlog\-format\-design.html
.TP
.B \-i pidlogfile
Specifies file where the pid of the process will be stored
.br
